{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Final rebar-debug report\n\nProblem: a package-free by-path load of reconcile.py raised ModuleNotFoundError when its re-exported binding-store commit helper ran.\n\nProven root cause: d9e0f0e733 changed the helper from package-independent git calls to an unconditional top-level rebar_reconciler.git_adapter import at reconcile_helpers.py:200. Standalone reconcile.py creates the loader child key and loads reconcile_helpers under a flat key, but does not create an importable parent package, so execution failed before the documented no-state True branch and fail-open catch.\n\nProof: the fresh-process trace entered line 200 and raised with find_spec(rebar_reconciler) returning None; it never reached the result branches. The exact historical probe was True at d9 parent and red from d9 onward. Package and engine_env routes stayed green, ruling out adapter behavior. Catch-widening experiments returned the wrong no-state result and could not perform commit-back, ruling out containment as repair.\n\nTest: tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_reconcile_helpers_standalone_git_adapter.py was collected and executed RED first under the CI marker gate. Its three isolated python -I subprocess cases all failed at the exact ModuleNotFoundError. The file was physically removed before the blind fixer ran, then restored GREEN at 3 passed. Re-seeding the exact old absolute import returned all three to RED; restoring the repair returned all three to GREEN. The oracle asserts return values, canonical adapter identity, adapter-boundary calls, and stderr diagnostics, so it is behavior-focused and refactor-tolerant.\n\nFix: _commit_binding_store_snapshot now resolves git_adapter through the existing _load helper with canonical key rebar_reconciler.git_adapter and sibling file git_adapter.py. This restores package-free loading while preserving cache/preseed identity and every existing git operation and True/False/error behavior.\n\nScope and safety: bounded callers are the reconcile.py re-export, one production call after binding-store save, and direct tests; none depended on the import failure. The fix restores pre-d9 behavior, adds no dependency or capability, and weakens no existing test. Only one production line and the held-out regression module changed.\n\nSiblings: the construct sweep covered every remaining absolute git_adapter import. The advisory-lock and ref-lock standalone defects are already repaired/tracked by fibrous-fabulous-dungbeetle; _concurrency is dispositioned by the pending design-classification ticket silt-resistant-gonolek; apply_outbound.py and __main__.py are package-context-only and are not siblings. No new undispositioned construct hit remains. Parity rule: binding-store snapshot commit-back preserves its boolean/error contract in package and standalone loading contexts. CLI and automated reconciliation converge through __main__.py:534 -> reconcile_once -> reconcile.py:668 -> this helper. MCP/API and public library expose no independent snapshot operation; there is no mirror-direction operation requiring the loader rule. No MISSING parity slot.\n\nResidual risk and prevention: unit-suite package pollution could mask this class; fixed in scope by the isolated python -I contract test. No other observed fragility remains undispositioned.\n\nReplication and gates: the exact fresh-process package-free reproduction now prints True. Focused helper/state tests: 10 passed. Full state suite: 355 passed. Full reconciler unit suite: 2775 passed. make lint passed, make typecheck passed, commit hooks passed, and local rebar review-code returned PASS with 0 blocking and 0 advisory findings. Commit a4309975d04e3528c8eb863383ebc7591a31610f carries DCO, Change-Id I2685bc10db4d2114b585fda4c6fd9feef4947b3c, and the canonical ticket trailer. Not pushed or closed while Change 1855 owns the serialized CI slot."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787053556021976001,"uuid":"1753520a-5c58-4c14-a769-f6a74187c9d7"}